    "denominator_semantics": "roster = the FULL workload denominator INCLUDING not-yet-built kernels; absent kernels stay in the denominator and pull coverage down (that is what makes C_dispatch a real target). A key's covered-state = best six-state across its variant rows (实验总纲 line 32).",
    "roster_notes": [
      "vec_dot: all 24 formats are class A (the ruling moved low-bit INTO the numerator). q1_0 (1-bit) and nvfp4 are in-code as their own monoliths -> default class A.",
      "product_reduce (3 decomposed shapes) are SEPARATE keys from vec_dot. q4_0 therefore appears twice: vec_dot/q4_0 (constructed-weak) AND product_reduce/q4_0_nibble (constructed strong). These are NOT merged.",
      "quantize_row roster = the activation quantizers {q8_0,q8_1,q8_K} (you quantize the activation to q8_x, not to every weight format). WIDTH LEVER: a human may widen.",
      "dequantize_row roster = per A-format (all 24 weight formats each have a row dequantizer). Only q5_0 is wired in-code today; the other 23 are absent and correctly pull coverage down. WIDTH LEVER (research escalation 5).",
      "gemm_tile RVV roster = per A-format (all 24) WIDE with unbuilt=absent, to expose the real gap: 5 formats {q4_0,q4_1,q4_K,q5_0,q8_0} have repack GEMM in-code; the other 19 are absent. WIDTH LEVER (research escalation 5).",
      "gemm_tile IME = the ratified aspirational triple {q4_0,q8_0,q4_K}. IME exposes a format-AGNOSTIC MMAOp/MMAUOp execution op, not a format-keyed tile -> these 3 keys are absent (roster goal, not an in-code op set).",
      "B class = all 9 forward ops (B-pending, not excluded): gelu/add/mul/cpy are absent in-code and stay in the denominator (honest C_dispatch, decision 3).",
      "C class = explicit defer (flash_attn tile, bf16 Zvfbfmin/bf16 roadmap X-line)."
    ]
